<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6298825d4ee96a07b93523c2f366527ae2be8a27" commit="71288f766bb753f2e2121431c5b88f4ff6a4fdba" commit_message="power: Provide chipset and board callbacks on host sleep event command  This change allows chipset and board to perform any action when host indicates intention to enter sleep state. Chipset can take action like enable/disable power signal interrupts and boards can enable/disable decay of VRs on host intent to enter/exit S0ix.  BUG=b:65732924 BRANCH=None TEST=make -j buildall  Change-Id: I6298825d4ee96a07b93523c2f366527ae2be8a27 Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/677498 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="677498" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/98/677498/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9c5afb408694b3b467e85dcea723f7574bc639c1" commit="75b7600b8d95dc3fd3743c36f50efbd93b5c7f86" commit_message="poppy: Dynamically disable effect of SLP_S0# on all VRs  Just setting the global VRMODECTRL register is not enough to disable the effect of SLP_S0# signal. Each VR control register needs to be set correctly to ignore the effect as well. However, disabling VR decay on SLP_S0# assertion by default results in additional power consumption during S0ix. In order to prevent this, VR decay on SLP_S0# assertion needs to be enabled and disabled dynamically as follows:  1. By default on EC boot, PMIC will be initialized to disable VR decay on SLP_S0# assertion. 2. When host indicates intent to enter S0ix, EC will enable decay of VRs on SLP_S0# assertion. 3. When host exits from S0ix and updates the intent to no longer enter S0ix using host command, EC will disable decay of VRs on SLP_S0# assertion.   actual SLP_S0# assertion because PMIC seems to honor the setting only  at SLP_S0# assertion and not if it is already asserted.  BUG=b:65732924 BRANCH=None TEST=Verified with this change that the failing Lux device is stable for a long time even with runtime S0ix.  Change-Id: I9c5afb408694b3b467e85dcea723f7574bc639c1 Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/674034 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="674034" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/34/674034/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7211ab554f4a6c156c1e8e79a3d9f0d6644217c6" commit="c66e225eccb840a94eb258ee87406380bb21615b" commit_message="Add WebUSB descriptor support  The WebUSB specification defines a specific Platform Descriptor in the Binary Object Store: https://wicg.github.io/webusb/#webusb-platform-capability-descriptor This descriptor provides a special 'Landing page' URL to the host browser and associated privileges for it.  Bump the USB version for BOS descriptors to 2.1 to be compatible with Chrome implementation.  Signed-off-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=none BRANCH=twinkie TEST=manual: on Twinkie (chip/stm32) and HG proto2 (chip/g), enumerate WebUSB descriptors with lsusb and connect to a WebUSB page in Chrome R61+.  Change-Id: I7211ab554f4a6c156c1e8e79a3d9f0d6644217c6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/664813 Commit-Ready: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="664813" owner_email="vpalatin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/13/664813/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3573852689bd51b437fe8f22994c499034266ace" commit="e5fca7cd175547ce1cb7561b4338b83932b8cf7a" commit_message="enter_chroot.sh: FILES_TO_COPY_TO_CHROOT += .inputrc  Preserve keyboard and other readline shortcuts when entering chroot.  BUG=none TEST=command line interactions don't change when entering chroot  Change-Id: I3573852689bd51b437fe8f22994c499034266ace Signed-off-by: Marc Herbert &lt;marc.herbert@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/677578 Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="677578" owner_email="marc.herbert@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosutils" ref="refs/changes/78/677578/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2ea64b542d4da470bd6347b13e064014d759ae33" commit="b57404ffb3bab1da01b5ce5433a7de11770951c6" commit_message="Update .clang-format file  Switch away from Brillo's clang-format file and make it work more like Chromium. See CL:677192 for the discussion.  BUG=chromium:767348 TEST=Ran clang-format on login_manager  Change-Id: I2ea64b542d4da470bd6347b13e064014d759ae33 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/678725 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="678725" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/25/678725/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I176f0d5c2eeb432cf198f438f2d893bf51a02